Reading: the wicket/residual part of z carries little between-player signal (tau 0.02 vs 0.06 for the runs part), so separate shrinkage damps it heavily (median shrink factor 0.2-0.3).
Shrinking the two parts separately is at least as repeatable as any alternative and, unlike one-number shrinkage, is stable; raw win-probability change is clearly worse.